  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Commercial electrified huayno of Peru's provincial cities and Lima migrant districts, emerging in the 1970s-80s as Junín and Ancash artists replaced harp and violin with electric guitar, Farfisa-type organ and drum kit, and reaching mass scale in the 1990s-2000s via cassette and later video-CD releases by Dina Páucar, Sonia Morales and Abencia Meza — retaining the pentatonic melody and 2/4 iambic huayno cell but adding sustained-chord backing, saxophone lines from the Junín orquesta típica and a heavily reverbed lead soprano.",
